- Just in passing.

00:00:17.746 --> 00:00:18.579
- Yes, yes.

00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:19.440
- [Niecy] So, but I'm happy we finally

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.080
have a chance to sit and chat.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.420
- Well, I'm so thankful
that you invited me to come

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.520
because I've been looking
forward to having,

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:27.990
be able to spend some time.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:28.823
You know, like I said,

00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:31.350
I've been aware of you for so, so long.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:33.360
I'm so proud of you and all
the things that you're doing.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.500
So, congrats on all the-

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.760
- Thank you.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.593
- Great stuff.

00:00:36.593 --> 00:00:37.426
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:37.426 --> 00:00:38.940
And so it's nice to be here with you.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:39.773
- Thank you.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:40.606
Thank you so much.

00:00:40.606 --> 00:00:42.270
Okay, so we,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.170
it's the New Year,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:47.040
so, are you a big resolutions guy?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.990
- I make resolutions every day,

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:50.760
that I try to get to (chuckles)

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:51.650
and I never keep.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.483
(Niecy laughs)

00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:53.316
(audience applauding)

00:00:53.316 --> 00:00:54.149
But yeah,

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:55.830
you know, my birthday is in December,

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:57.510
Christmas, New Year,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.760
and I come up with all these resolutions,

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.763
and I'm good for about six weeks.

00:01:01.763 --> 00:01:02.970
(audience laughs)

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:04.770
About six weeks.
- And then you just fall off?

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.480
- And then it's just, it's over.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.313
It's over.

00:01:07.313 --> 00:01:08.730
I can't talk myself into it.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:12.840
There's a part of me that's
always resisting and so,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.669
but six weeks I can really, kind of,

00:01:14.669 --> 00:01:16.530
get back in shape and, you know

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.810
I'm gonna do it forever and
of course it doesn't last.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.940
- Okay, so then what resolutions

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.710
have you made for this go around?

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:24.360
- Well, this coming year,

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.390
there's a Kenneth C. Davis has a book,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.400
about 52 books,

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.050
a book a week for a year.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.830
And I realize, now that I'm older,

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.960
there's so many things
that I haven't read,

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.260
and I'm gonna read a book each week.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.200
Hopefully I'll last for
more than six weeks, but.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.486
- A book a week?

00:01:44.486 --> 00:01:45.319
(audience applauding)

00:01:45.319 --> 00:01:46.920
- Yeah. I think that-

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.760
- [Niecy] Wow.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.953
- You know, when you have time,

00:01:51.189 --> 00:01:52.022
and when I was younger,

00:01:52.022 --> 00:01:54.480
I was so busy trying to
build my career and family,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.560
and the kids are small.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.960
Now I have time to really sort of,

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.517
take a look at the world and just-

00:01:59.517 --> 00:02:01.948
- And it's more of a luxury for you.

00:02:01.948 --> 00:02:02.781
- Yeah, yeah.

00:02:02.781 --> 00:02:04.590
- See, you know what? And
for me, when I was younger

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.760
it was a punishment.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:07.357
If I was acting up, my mother would say,

00:02:07.357 --> 00:02:08.450
"Go read a book."

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.283
(audience laughs)

00:02:09.283 --> 00:02:10.590
And then I'm like-
- Yeah.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.423
- You know?
- Right.

00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:14.400
- So I don't know if I
had the same idea about it

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.399
as I do now, as an adult, yeah.

00:02:16.399 --> 00:02:17.232
- That's what I'm saying.

00:02:17.232 --> 00:02:19.350
Now you can actually do it
because you want to do it

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.950
and you realize the value of it.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.783
- You know what?

00:02:21.783 --> 00:02:24.080
I love your speaking voice.

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:24.913
- [Ernie] Oh.

00:02:24.913 --> 00:02:26.600
- It has such texture and-

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.433
- Oh, well, thank you.

00:02:27.433 --> 00:02:28.266
- [Niecy] And depth.

00:02:28.266 --> 00:02:29.932
- Oh
- [Niecy] Yeah. I like that.

00:02:29.932 --> 00:02:30.900
- You know, it doesn't
sound the way to me.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:32.637
It sounds like it's up here.

00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:33.470
(audience laughs)

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:34.800
But, thank you.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.800
- Well, see, listen.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.280
When you have a voice,

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.900
'cause I have a unique voice, too.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.733
- [Ernie] Right.

00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:42.872
- And I sound like I need
to drink a glass of lotion.

00:02:42.872 --> 00:02:43.705
(audience laughs)

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:44.580
You know?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.970
And I've had this same
voice since a little girl.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:48.803
Can you imagine?

00:02:48.803 --> 00:02:49.636
(Ernie chuckles)

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.469
You know what I mean?

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:51.302
They were like,

00:02:51.302 --> 00:02:52.255
"Little girl, do you smoke cigarettes?"

00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:53.481
(Ernie audience laughing)

00:02:53.481 --> 00:02:54.900
(Niecy chuckles)

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.170
But, do you ever use, like, your voice?

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.120
Do you take advantage of
having such a great voice?

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:00.953
- Well, as an actor,

00:03:00.953 --> 00:03:02.160
that's part of the, you know,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.080
this is what we have to work with.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:04.913
But sometimes,

00:03:04.913 --> 00:03:06.660
which, I think I have a nice voice,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.920
but sometimes it works against you.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:10.927
I was doing a commercial
in New York and they said,

00:03:10.927 --> 00:03:11.760
"No, stop, stop.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.340
It's, your voice. It's too sexy."

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.316
- Sexy? Whoo!

00:03:15.316 --> 00:03:17.128
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:03:17.128 --> 00:03:19.091
- And I said, they said,

00:03:19.091 --> 00:03:21.330
"We don't want that. We don't want that.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:23.010
Just do it."

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.170
So, but then the next week,

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.827
I had an audition for

00:03:26.827 --> 00:03:29.070
"Star Trek: Deep Space Nine"

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:30.780
that Avery Brooks finally did.

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:31.613
- Uh huh.

00:03:31.613 --> 00:03:32.446
- And I went in,

00:03:32.446 --> 00:03:33.697
I did great on the audition and they said,

00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:34.740
"Have Ernie come back,

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.688
but this time, tell him to be sexier."

00:03:36.688 --> 00:03:37.602
- [Niecy] Ooh.

00:03:37.602 --> 00:03:38.435
(audience chuckles)

00:03:38.435 --> 00:03:40.440
- So how do you be sexier?

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.480
I don't know. But the guy
said I had a sexy voice,

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.580
so I went in and I said, "Hey, y'all."

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.569
And they said, "Ernie, stop."

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:46.402
(audience laughs)

00:03:46.402 --> 00:03:47.436
"Stop."

00:03:47.436 --> 00:03:48.269
(Niecy laughs)

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:49.102
"Thank you very much.

00:03:49.102 --> 00:03:50.010
You can leave now."

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.327
So, apparently, it wasn't that sexy.

00:03:51.327 --> 00:03:53.905
- It wasn't so sexy that time.

00:03:53.905 --> 00:03:57.060
- But your sound is so much a part of you.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.850
I do a lot of voiceovers
and I like to change,

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.610
because our sound does sort of,

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:03.810
identify who we are.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.648
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:04:04.648 --> 00:04:06.345
(audience applauding)

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:10.230
- So, for fans of your
show "Quantum Leap,"

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.000
how are things going over there?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:12.833
- It's going great.

00:04:12.833 --> 00:04:14.820
We got the pickup for the full season.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:15.653
- Yes!

00:04:15.653 --> 00:04:16.950
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.680
- It's definitely one of the most amazing,

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:21.600
fun shows I've ever worked on.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.810
I've been doing this
for 50 plus seven years.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.520
But, it's a great show,

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.720
and it's a great cast,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.062
and I'm so excited to be
a part of it, you know?

00:04:30.062 --> 00:04:31.305
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:04:31.305 --> 00:04:32.138
- Yeah.

00:04:33.013 --> 00:04:36.480
So, the show involves time travel.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.313
- Yes.

00:04:37.313 --> 00:04:40.113
- Now, if you could really
go back to any time,

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.230
where would you wanna land?

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.760
- Well, you know,

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.380
that's a big question.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:49.410
For me, I know I got here some way,

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.340
but I've never met my mom or my dad.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.040
- Hmm.
- And I would love to,

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.109
I know it happened because I'm here

00:04:55.109 --> 00:04:56.490
(audience laughs)

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.050
and I would love to,

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.470
not go back and be in one of them,

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.480
but maybe a close friend,

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.760
and see how they, who were these people?

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:06.900
How did they come together?

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.130
How did they,

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:09.450
how did they, you know,

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.630
create me and, yeah, so.

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.844
- Okay. I'm with that.

00:05:13.844 --> 00:05:14.677
(audience applauding)

00:05:14.677 --> 00:05:15.510
- I'd like to-

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:16.411
- I'm with that.

00:05:16.411 --> 00:05:17.457
Okay.

00:05:17.457 --> 00:05:22.457
So, you've been working in
film and TV for over 45 years.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.043
Yeah.
- And, yes. Yes.

00:05:24.043 --> 00:05:25.611
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:05:25.611 --> 00:05:26.606
- Yep.

00:05:26.606 --> 00:05:27.439
- Yeah.

00:05:27.439 --> 00:05:31.320
- And a lot of young actors,
I'm sure look up to you.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.960
Was there ever a time when
you felt like giving up

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.280
or throwing in the towel?

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:36.113
- Oh, yeah.

00:05:36.113 --> 00:05:37.200
There's been a number of times

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.000
when you just think
you've just hit that wall.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.800
But, you know, my grandmother said,

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.630
putting out your faith in man,

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:45.450
you know, God, the universe that I trust-

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.705
- Yes.

00:05:46.705 --> 00:05:47.538
- I remember I first came out to LA

00:05:47.538 --> 00:05:48.978
and it was a real hard time.

00:05:48.978 --> 00:05:49.811
I borrowed,

00:05:49.811 --> 00:05:51.539
I was doing a play with Nichelle Nichols.

00:05:51.539 --> 00:05:52.620
- [Niecy] Oh, yes.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.800
- And, we had a rehearsal at
her house in Beverly Hills.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.720
So I drove my car to Beverly Hills,

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.730
hoping I had enough gas
to get there and back.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:00.563
- Oh, yeah.

00:06:00.563 --> 00:06:02.190
- And when I got there,

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:06.240
I took a seat on the
steps inside the house,

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.073
but when I looked down,

00:06:07.073 --> 00:06:09.210
there was a quarter on the floor.

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:11.478
And I wanted to take that quarter so bad.

00:06:11.478 --> 00:06:12.435
(Ernie chuckles)

00:06:12.435 --> 00:06:14.279
- Oh.

00:06:14.279 --> 00:06:16.320
- And, but I didn't. I didn't.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:17.986
I thought, "No, it doesn't belong to me."

00:06:17.986 --> 00:06:20.052
But man, I could use that quarter, but.

00:06:20.052 --> 00:06:22.110
(audience laughs)

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:22.943
So, yeah.

00:06:22.943 --> 00:06:24.510
And she and I, we laughed about it.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.220
She was just an amazing lady

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:27.540
and a wonderful, wonderful person, but.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.290
- See, but it's those
kind of humble beginnings-

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.123
- [Ernie] Yeah.

00:06:32.123 --> 00:06:32.956
(audience applauding)

00:06:32.956 --> 00:06:35.460
- That make you appreciate
all that we have right now.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.293
- Absolutely. Absolutely, yeah.

00:06:36.293 --> 00:06:37.770
- You know, listen,

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:39.900
I remember being in a room,

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.880
you know, auditioning for a part,

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:44.309
and this was back when they
used to give you talent holds.

00:06:44.309 --> 00:06:45.142
- Yeah. (chuckles)

00:06:45.142 --> 00:06:46.980
- They would just give you
a bag of money to sit around

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:48.481
until they found something to do with you.

00:06:48.481 --> 00:06:49.314
(audience laughs)

00:06:49.314 --> 00:06:50.730
And let me tell you what.

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:53.274
They were talking about
me as if I were not there.

00:06:53.274 --> 00:06:54.107
- [Ernie] Right.

00:06:54.107 --> 00:06:55.770
- I was down to my last.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.730
You know, and I already had children

00:06:59.379 --> 00:07:00.720
and my last few bucks.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:01.553
And they were like,

00:07:01.553 --> 00:07:03.180
"Well how much you think
we should give her?"

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.013
And, you know,

00:07:04.013 --> 00:07:05.910
and they were going back
and forth with the number.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:07.147
And I said,

00:07:07.147 --> 00:07:08.829
"Do they know I could hear them?"

00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:09.662
(audience laughs)

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:10.950
"I can hear you."

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.870
Baby, they hit a good number,

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:15.510
and they agreed on it
right in front of my face.

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.310
And when I tell you I
ran around that office

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.510
and caught the Holy Ghost,

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.343
they said,

00:07:19.343 --> 00:07:20.531
"We better get this girl outta here."

00:07:20.531 --> 00:07:21.480
(audience laughs)

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:23.393
I said, "Can I get the money today?"

00:07:23.393 --> 00:07:26.007
(audience applauding)

00:07:26.007 --> 00:07:27.135
- Yeah.

00:07:27.135 --> 00:07:28.320
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.153
- So, what was the,

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:33.878
what was the first big
thing you booked and then,

00:07:33.878 --> 00:07:36.150
how did you celebrate it?

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.280
- Well, the first big thing was with,

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:42.070
Gordon Parks gave me a part
in a movie called "Leadbelly."

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:43.680
- Mm hm.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:45.690
- And I was one of the first people cast,

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.587
and the producer who, he said,

00:07:47.587 --> 00:07:48.960
"Well, Gordon likes you.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.853
We're gonna give you $605 a week.

00:07:50.853 --> 00:07:51.750
How's that?"

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:52.960
And I'm like, "600, yeah!"

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:53.793
(Niecy laughs)

00:07:53.793 --> 00:07:56.340
Well, the minimum was $604.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:57.420
So it was like,

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.070
I found that out later on.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.360
But, you know,

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.877
I was a single dad to my two older boys,

00:08:03.877 --> 00:08:07.192
and celebration was just
being able to go home,

00:08:07.192 --> 00:08:09.120
and me and the boys would, you know,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.290
the rent's paid,

00:08:10.290 --> 00:08:12.325
we can keep the phone on a little longer,

00:08:12.325 --> 00:08:13.158
you know?

00:08:13.158 --> 00:08:14.547
- Well, you know, now,

00:08:14.547 --> 00:08:15.900
now you should treat yourself.

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.460
Every time you get a new job,

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.720
buy yourself a little something.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:19.650
That's how I live.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.580
- Yeah.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:21.413
That's, yeah.

